// REJECTS: Field 'port' is required
//
// A Static datasource specification requires all three of name, host and port. The grammar
// asks for none of them -- `STATIC_DSP BRACE_OPEN (dbName | dbHost | dbPort)* BRACE_CLOSE`
// admits an empty body -- so every one of the three is a walker rule.
//
// A generated parser therefore accepts `Static { }`, and so does anything that models these
// blocks as bags of optional settings. Which fields are required varies per specification
// kind (LocalH2 requires nothing, EmbeddedH2 requires name, directory and autoServerMode),
// so there is no single default a rewrite can fall back on.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::StaticNoPort
{
   store: fixture::neg::Db;
   type: SqlServer;
   specification: Static
   {
      name: 'db';
      host: 'host';
   };
   auth: DefaultH2;
}
